      id: "hook-31", type: "hook",
      content: "The NCW can summon a Chief Secretary, put him on oath, demand his files, and after inquiry tell the government to prosecute an offender — and the government can simply ignore it. That is the whole paradox: civil court powers of investigation attached to recommendations with no binding force. Which is why every serious debate about the NCW since 2020 has converged on one demand — constitutional status, like the SC Commission under Article 338 and the ST Commission under Article 338A.",
