      content: "The NCW is a STATUTORY body established in 1992 under the National Commission for Women Act, 1990 — India's apex watchdog on women's rights — comprising a Chairperson + 5 Members + a Member-Secretary appointed by the Central Government for 3 years, exercising civil court powers under the CPC 1908 as a quasi-judicial body whose recommendations are NOT legally binding; hence the persistent demand to confer constitutional status on it, on the model of Articles 338 and 338A.",
